			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "696ee1e5-7035-4250-b038-2129f8aba92d")
	)
	(text "U16 isolates A1 S2 TX from CM4 GPIO13 (ROBO_RX_MCU); U19 (below the\nJ9 box) isolates CM4 GPIO12 (ROBO_TX_MCU) from A1 S1 RX and its pull-up.\nA1 runs from the battery while the CM4 can be off (SW1 open, GLOBAL_EN\npower cycle). Wired direct, A1 would back-power the CM4 through GPIO13\nor GPIO12 (abs max VREF+0.5 V). Both 74LVC1G17 run on 3V3_CM4; with it\noff, Ioff makes Y high-Z and A tolerates 3.3 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 289.05 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7af8d9e9-dad1-4333-adee-572b24a8eed3")
	)
	(text "D23: Vishay SMBJ3V3-E3/52, 600 W\nSMB TVS. VBR >= 4.1 V, VC 7.3 V\n@ 50 A, IR <= 200 uA. Holds U18 OUT\n(7 V abs max) on a J9 miswire until\nF3 trips. Not a generic SMBJ3.3A:\nsome break down at 6.5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 166.37 151.765 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7b4580f3-9ec3-450b-8b37-1aa7f8b94fa4")
	)
	(text "2V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 157.48 95.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "83f06ada-379f-4af0-841d-08b4930360c8")
	)
	(text "JUMPERS  (ENC1: JP1 JP2 JP3, ENC2: JP4 JP5 JP6)\nJP1/JP4  V+ supply   1-2: 5 V (RC_5V)\n                     3-4: 3.3 V (ENC_3V3, U18)\n                     5-6: 12 V (ENC_12V, battery)\n         Shunt across a row only: 1-3 or 3-5 shorts two rails.\nJP2/JP5  mode        1-3 + 2-4: QUAD\n                     3-5 + 4-6: ABS\nJP3/JP6  ABS scale   1-2: 3.3 V sensor -> 2 V\n                     2-3: 0-2 V direct\nDefault ENC1 (Firgelli): 5V, QUAD\nDefault ENC2 (AS5600): 3.3V, ABS, 3V3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 207.01 156.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8a6575c6-cf13-4a22-98fd-1d6d045026ca")
	)
	(text "LIMIT SWITCHES: the RoboClaw has one limit input per motor (S4 = M1, S5 = M2) and supports two\nswitches on it. Wire two NC switches in SERIES per axis (J12 elevation, J13 azimuth): either one\nopening lets the 4.7k pull-up raise the input. Set Invert (active-high). Both switches share the\npin, so the RoboClaw takes fwd/rev from the commanded direction: set S4/S5 to Limit(Both), or to\nHome(User)/Limit(Fwd) with the retract-end switch on the reverse side so it also zeroes the\nencoder (elevation, Firgelli). NO switches would go in parallel instead. J12/J13 are 2-pin:\ndaisy-chain the second switch in the field wiring.\nThe E-stop and limit loops run at 12 V (ENC_12V): R48/R52/R55 4.7k pull-ups pass about 2.6 mA through the closed contacts\n(contact wetting on long cable runs); open, the node sits at battery voltage (10-14.6 V) and the 47k/20k\ndivider (R50/R109, R54/R107, R56/R108) delivers 3.0-4.4 V to S3/S4/S5 (5 V tolerant); C58/C60/C61 10 nF, tau 0.14 ms.\nD17/D19/D20 are 15 V ESD parts for the 12 V nodes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 238.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8f405950-873e-40c0-a4e1-6895e9573a28")
	)
	(text "EMC: run motor leads in shielded cable, shield\nclamped 360 deg to the enclosure at the gland\n(not to J11/J14). Clip-on CM ferrite per pair at\nentry; 100 nF brush caps at the motors. Keep\nmotor leads away from GNSS/encoder wiring."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.088 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9e250d5e-0632-4b07-b02f-ea2918db1f2e")
	)
	(text "J11 = Firgelli motor (elevation):\n1 BLUE  (+)\n2 BROWN (-)\nSwap to reverse, or\ninvert M1 in Motion Studio."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 73.66 172.212 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a361fa3d-1da6-4189-884d-7e1b4cfbdd92")
	)
	(text "ABS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b239fe31-f433-4568-a585-b878091266cf")
	)
	(text "E-stop and limits: 12 V loops, NC,\nset Invert. 2 limits/motor: see note."
